# Media rules

## Source safety

- Probe input media before processing.
- Never overwrite original Episode input/source files.
- Record failures; never convert a non-zero media failure into publish success.

## Canvas / mobile evidence

- Default video canvas: 1080×1920, 30fps.
- Horizontal recordings use `screen_focus`, `screen_stack`, `roi_crop` or another explicit mobile-readable composition.
- Full landscape contain with black bars is not a publish layout.
- ROI crops are allowed and expected when they improve evidence readability; use an establishing shot when surrounding context is necessary.

## Audio / timing

- Follow `config/voice.yaml`.
- Do not pick a random TTS provider for final narration.
- Accepted final narration is the timing master.
- Generate subtitle/word timestamps from final audio; never estimate cue timing from text length.
- Avoid clipping; duck BGM/SFX under narration.

## Motion / renderers

Read `docs/video-plugin-routing.md` to choose a capability **only when needed**.
HyperFrames/Remotion/ChatCut/CapCut/Jianying/etc. are bounded tools, not workflow authorities.

## QA

Technical validity is necessary but insufficient. Creator Review must inspect the actual artifact/mobile preview. Only `READY_TO_PUBLISH` permits `FINAL.*` naming.
